;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Reducible: nth traps out of range), §1.2 P5; plan §6 L5a (RangeLen is the element type's contract)
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   nth: index out of range
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; The integer instances of range-nth check the index against the count themselves, negative ones included,
;; for the same reason as case 184: they are called by users of the protocol as well as by nth.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq))

(defun main () -> i64 (range-nth 0 10 3 -1))
